Cell["\<\
By manipulating the parameter value of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]c\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], we see that for sufficiently small c term1 yields \
negative values. 
n amplifies the impact. 
A higher alpha expands the domain for c such that term1 yields negative values.
Some examples obtained using the manipulation and depicting graph for \
different alpha values:
alpha = 0.3, for all c < 0.6, term1 < 0; For c around 0.6+, term1 gets \
negative values for small n but positive values for large n.
alpha = 0.5, for all c < 1, term1 < 0; Similar argument above applies here \
and for the conditions below.
alpha = 0.6, for all c < 1.2, term1 < 0
alpha = 0.7, for all c < 1.4, term1 < 0
alpha = 0.8, for all c < 1.6, term1 < 0 though the impact of n is \
non-monotonic.
What about the smallest possible alpha?
Allowing for two-digits after comma, the smallest alpha that still produces \
term1 < 0 is 0.06. For all c < 0.12, term1 <  0.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.905903515060871*^9, 
  3.90590354545267*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"68517cbd-4163-4c6a-aeb6-\
b4af4e9b671a"],

Cell["\<\
For the existence of stable grand coalition with interior optimal efforts, we \
need to provide one example. 
Take b=0.0309, c = 1.01, n = 10, alpha = 0.5, and eta = 0.8 . 
The term1 and hence the condition U_s(N) \[GreaterEqual] U_n(N-1) holds:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9059036456234407`*^9, 3.9059037136299353`*^9}, {
  3.905903788254964*^9, 
  3.905903834224419*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"702d812f-7734-4c94-aa84-\
664e59ae7d0a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"term1", "[", 
  RowBox[{"1.01", ",", "10", ",", "0.5"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[89]:=",ExpressionUUID->"769fd2bc-8fd4-4b6b-bcf0-e75bac4a90bc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"-", "0.2941369999999992`"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.905903697262323*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[89]=",ExpressionUUID->"56b526d7-f1bb-4190-b556-44fd19813e93"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["And we have interior solutions at the grand coalition:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.905903843545657*^9, 3.9059038487088842`*^9}, {
  3.905903916490744*^9, 
  3.905903921643051*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"aaa2a109-eb98-4a4f-ba6e-\
5e619df071ae"],

